{"audio":{"src":"https://pub-13abeb101e2945d2a7f60234f6faf52e.r2.dev/materials/2026-07-16-table-tennis-spin-serves-history-and-two-great-players/audio/main-74555b7753ec.mp3","durationSec":130.32,"cues":[{"start":0,"end":2.44,"text":"Players brush the ball with the racket to make spin."},{"start":3.38,"end":7.65,"text":"The three basic kinds are topspin, backspin, and sidespin."},{"start":7.65,"end":11.7,"text":"Topspin makes the ball dip and move forward quickly after the bounce."},{"start":11.7,"end":14.62,"text":"Backspin can make it stay low and slow."},{"start":14.62,"end":17.42,"text":"Sidespin can make it curve left or right."},{"start":18.32,"end":20.82,"text":"Spin is often hard to see before the bounce."},{"start":21.48,"end":24.48,"text":"Its effect is easier to see after the ball hits the table."},{"start":25.12,"end":27.98,"text":"A player watches the bounce and changes the next shot."},{"start":28.54,"end":30.4,"text":"Every point starts with a serve."},{"start":31.14,"end":33.84,"text":"In an official serve, the ball begins on an open palm."},{"start":34.36,"end":38.72,"text":"The server tosses it nearly straight up at least 16 centimetres."},{"start":38.72,"end":40.46,"text":"The server hits the ball as it falls."},{"start":41.14,"end":43.84,"text":"The ball first bounces on the server’s side of the table."},{"start":44.28,"end":45.8,"text":"Then it bounces on the other side."},{"start":46.38,"end":49.44,"text":"A server can change the speed, place, and spin."},{"start":50.16,"end":52.5,"text":"These changes can make the next shot difficult."},{"start":53.06,"end":58.68,"text":"A short backspin serve and a fast topspin serve can start two very different points."},{"start":58.68,"end":63.4,"text":"Table tennis began in England in the 1880s."},{"start":63.68,"end":66.46,"text":"People played it as an indoor form of lawn tennis."},{"start":67.14,"end":70.34,"text":"They used a dining table and simple equipment they had around them."},{"start":70.96,"end":73.38,"text":"The sport later became more organised."},{"start":73.38,"end":78,"text":"The International Table Tennis Federation, or ITTF, began in 1926."},{"start":78.72,"end":83.32,"text":"The first World Championships also took place in 1926, in London."},{"start":84.32,"end":87.54,"text":"A game for indoor tables had become an international sport."},{"start":88.3,"end":92.76,"text":"Today, the table is still small, but players compete around the world."},{"start":94.8,"end":96.3,"text":"Ma Long represents China."},{"start":97.02,"end":101.58,"text":"He won the Olympic men’s singles title in 2016 and again at Tokyo 2020."},{"start":102.74,"end":106.7,"text":"He became the first man to win this Olympic singles title twice."},{"start":108.54,"end":110.46,"text":"Mima Ito represents Japan."},{"start":110.46,"end":117.02,"text":"At Tokyo 2020, she and Jun Mizutani won the first Olympic mixed doubles table tennis title."},{"start":117.82,"end":121.04,"text":"It was also Japan’s first Olympic gold medal in table tennis."},{"start":122.14,"end":125.28,"text":"Ma Long’s result shows success across two Olympic Games."},{"start":126.34,"end":129.8,"text":"Mima Ito’s result marks two important firsts in one event."}],"words":[{"text":"Players","start":0,"end":0.32},{"text":"brush","start":0.32,"end":0.58},{"text":"the","start":0.58,"end":0.8},{"text":"ball","start":0.8,"end":0.94},{"text":"with","start":0.94,"end":1.1},{"text":"the","start":1.1,"end":1.24},{"text":"racket","start":1.24,"end":1.54},{"text":"to","start":1.54,"end":1.86},{"text":"make","start":1.86,"end":2.02},{"text":"spin","start":2.02,"end":2.44},{"text":"The","start":3.38,"end":3.5},{"text":"three","start":3.5,"end":3.74},{"text":"basic","start":3.74,"end":4.08},{"text":"kinds","start":4.08,"end":4.44},{"text":"are","start":4.44,"end":4.72},{"text":"topspin","start":4.72,"end":5.64},{"text":"backspin","start":5.64,"end":6.56},{"text":"and","start":6.56,"end":6.64},{"text":"sidespin","start":6.64,"end":7.6